# Agent debug artifacts — files agents create during "verification".
# These must NEVER be committed. If git add catches one, .gitignore stops it.
# If an agent commits via git add -A on already-tracked files, the agent has bug.
output.txt
debug-*.png
screenshot-*.png
test-telegram-*.mjs
test-telegram-*.js
apps/e2e/debug-*.png
apps/e2e/screenshot-*.png
apps/e2e/test-*.mjs
apps/e2e/test-*.js
apps/e2e/temp-*
apps/e2e/scratch-*

# Visual verification screenshots (PM/agents save locally; do not commit to repo)
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
.claude/tasks/*.png

# Session scratch: task briefs and harness counters.
#
# Task files are dispatch briefs written for one agent run. 39 of them were
# committed before this rule and stay tracked (git ignores untracked files
# only) — this stops NEW ones from accumulating as permanent untracked noise
# that shows up in every branch's pending-changes view. 40 had piled up by
# 2026-08-04.
#
# Consequence to know when dispatching: an ignored task file exists only in the
# main working copy, not in a fresh worktree. Keep passing agents the absolute
# path into the main repo (already the established practice) rather than a
# repo-relative one.
.claude/suggest-compact.counter
.claude/tasks/*.md
# ...кроме двух накопительных артефактов: они переживают отдельные задачи и
# нужны следующей сессии. Остальное в этом каталоге — рабочие черновики.
!.claude/tasks/BACKLOG-followups.md
!.claude/tasks/HANDOFF-*.md

# QA / manual-qa screenshots and local test configs (agent artifacts)
qa-screenshots/
manual-qa-screenshots/
apps/web/.env.qa
apps/web/vite.qa.config.ts
.claude/tasks/*.jpg
.claude/tasks/*.jpeg
# Whitelist legitimate assets under apps/web/public/ (favicon, og-image, etc.)
!apps/web/public/**/*.png
!apps/web/public/**/*.jpg
!apps/web/public/**/*.jpeg

# Claude Design sync workspace + bundle output (regenerable via /design-sync;
# CLI scaffolding with its own node_modules — NEVER commit). See
# .claude/skills/claude-design-workflow/.
.ds-sync/
ds-bundle/

# signal-plus (services/signal-plus/, Python — not a pnpm workspace member):
# secrets, mutable local state and the signal-cli data volume never belong in
# git, per task-signal-plus-service.md step 1.
services/signal-plus/.env
services/signal-plus/state*.json
services/signal-plus/data/
# Standard Python build/test hygiene for this one Python package in an
# otherwise all-TS repo — not explicitly requested by the task, but omitting
# it means __pycache__/.pytest_cache show up as untracked cruft on every
# future commit here; narrowly scoped to this directory so it cannot affect
# any other package.
services/signal-plus/**/__pycache__/
services/signal-plus/**/*.pyc
services/signal-plus/.pytest_cache/
services/signal-plus/*.egg-info/
